{"name":"Tobago","hex":"#44362d","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Tobago","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["An island and ward of the Caribbean, part of Trinidad and Tobago."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Tobago"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tobago","blocks":[{"text":"Tobago, officially the Ward of Tobago, is an island and ward in Trinidad and Tobago. It is 35 kilometres northeast of the larger island of Trinidad and about 160 kilometres off Venezuela's northeastern coast. It is southeast of Grenada and southwest of Barbados."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Td-map.png/330px-Td-map.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tobago","wikidata":"Q185111"},{"title":"Tobago (1793 ship)","blocks":[{"text":"Tobago was a ship launched in 1790. She came into British hands in 1793 and was probably a prize taken immediately after the outbreak of the French Revolutionary Wars in early 1793. She traded with Tobago for several years before new owners purchased her for whaling. She made two whaling voyages to the East Coast of Africa before her owners sold her to new owners. She then made two voyages as a slave ship. She was abandoned or condemned in 1802 after having delivered her captives on her second such voyage."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tobago_(1793_ship)","wikidata":"Q28136550"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Caribbean_-_Tobago.PNG/500px-Caribbean_-_Tobago.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Caribbean_-_Tobago.PNG/500px-Caribbean_-_Tobago.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACaribbean_-_Tobago.PNG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb